Fixed #1020 and committed as 6fb26bd6, with "Fixes #1020" in the title. With --max-tokens 32000, yoyo no longer tells bedrock or google users to lower it to their provider's default (16000 / 8192) as if that were the model's limit.

The change. There is now one function, declared_output_ceiling, in src/agent_builder.rs, and all four provider branches of build_agent call it. It returns "unknown" (None) for google and bedrock, and an unknown ceiling means no warning. For anthropic and the OpenAI-compatible providers it calls the same functions as before (the #964 and #1019 fixes), so their results are unchanged.

Where the fix sits. It's per branch, through that one shared function. The warning function itself has only one production caller, and it receives a number without knowing whether it's a default or a real maximum, so the fix couldn't go there.

Live check with the built binary, before and after:
• **bedrock:** the "declared output ceiling 16000" warning is gone. The run then fails on authentication (no AWS key), which is expected.
• **google:** the "ceiling 8192" warning is gone. The run fails with a 400 because there's no key, also expected.
• **anthropic** (claude-opus-5-5, --max-tokens 131072): still warns about the 128000 limit, with the same text.

Tests. They're in a new file, src/output_ceiling_tests.rs, rather than agent_builder.rs as the task said, because that file is 55 lines below the point where its size check fails. They build the warning the same way build_agent does:
• bedrock and google at 32000 produce no warning, and each test first checks that the old code would have warned.
• anthropic at 131072 and gpt-6-sol at 200000 still produce the exact warning text.
• A weak check on the source confirms build_agent calls the function exactly 4 times and no longer passes the default directly. It shows the calls are there, not that they're correct.

I ran two deliberate breakages, one at a time, each marked NEUTERED and undone in the same command. Putting bedrock's old line back in build_agent made the source check fail. Making the function return bedrock's default made the bedrock/google test fail. Both were restored, and no NEUTERED marker is left.

Docs and leftover work:
• I added a #1020 note to agent_builder.rs's entry in ARCHITECTURE.md.
• In that same entry, the #964 note still called the 128000/4096 fallback "the correct reading" for providers with unknown limits. #1019 had already made that false, so I marked it superseded where it stands.
• **#1021 (filed):** the google default model and the list of known gemini ids are out of date. I checked Google's model page myself: `gemini-3.0-pro` and `gemini-3.0-flash` appear 0 times there, but yoyo still lists both. I could not confirm the assessment's claim that 2.5 is restricted to returning users and retires on Vertex on 2026-10-20, and the issue says so.
• No google or bedrock setting currently records a real output maximum, so these providers now never get this warning. It stays off until a real maximum is recorded for them.

